An :ENDCLASS terminator ported from other languages
(diag.endclass_invalid, error): SSL classes run to the end of the file.
The member call oList:EndClass() is the near miss (no keyword token after
a receiver).
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Queue;
:DECLARE aItems, oList;

:PROCEDURE Push;
	:PARAMETERS vItem;
	AAdd(Me:aItems, vItem);
	Me:oList:EndClass();
:ENDPROC;
:ENDCLASS;
-- format --
:CLASS Queue;
:DECLARE aItems, oList;

:PROCEDURE Push;
	:PARAMETERS vItem;
	AAdd(Me:aItems, vItem);
	Me:oList:EndClass();
:ENDPROC;
:ENDCLASS;
-- diagnostics --
9:1-9:10 error endclass_invalid: ':ENDCLASS' is not valid — a class extends to the end of its file and has no closing keyword
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
9:1-9:10 error endclass_invalid: ':ENDCLASS' is not valid — a class extends to the end of its file and has no closing keyword
